<BaseLayout title="Accessibility and preferences" description="Grafito editorial accessibility preferences, evaluation scope, known limitations and a direct non-oral reporting channel." equivalent="/es/accessibility/"><div class="shell page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Access is part of the design</p><h1>Make the site work for you.</h1><p>Target: WCAG 2.2 A and AA. This is a development statement, not a claim of complete conformance. All essential editorial content is intended to remain available without an accessibility mode.</p></div><div class="shell prose"><PreferencesForm/><section><h2>Evaluation and limitations</h2><p>Last documentation review: <time datetime="2026-10-18">18 October 2026</time>. Automated checks cover token pairs, browser interactions and selected rendered states in the version’s local Windows test report. Tests with real screen readers, voice control, real browser zoom and user participation require separate evidence and remain pending unless the report identifies a completed session.</p><p>No embedded audiovisual material is supplied without reviewed subtitles, transcript and the necessary visual description. External journals and social networks are outside our control. Scientific notes retain structured mathematics; compatibility with particular assistive technologies needs manual verification.</p><p>If both persistent and session storage are blocked, preferences apply only to the current page. Reloading or following a full-document link can restore system defaults. No preferences are sent to a server or placed in URLs.</p></section><section><h2>Report a barrier</h2><p>Send the page address, the task you attempted and the difficulty to <a href="mailto:isaac.daroch.ormeno@gmail.com">Isaac Daroch by email</a>. You do not need to disclose a diagnosis, create an account or make a telephone call. Do not send medical data or passwords.</p><p><a href="/explore/">Use the site map</a> to find another route to the content.</p></section></div></BaseLayout>
